   "author": "Hollowmere team",
   "story": "Ezra Vane climbed poles for the county for thirty-one years before a bar fight and a judge put him in the Remand Program. They dropped him two runs before you. He found the line truck where its crew had left it, half off the line road, and lived out of it all summer, climbing poles to cut the dead lines down so they couldn't spark the timber. In August a pole he was topping gave way under him. He splinted his own leg, dragged the pole across the open side of the truck, strung a tarp and kept the fire going. He has been waiting for someone with a first aid kit ever since.",
